But std.unicode.utf8Decode returns usize? Let's check Zig 0.16 docs: std.unicode.utf8Decode(bytes: []const u8, codepoint: *u21) usize. It returns number of bytes consumed. So we need to pass pointer to cp. So:

var cp: u21 = 0;
const len = std.unicode.utf8Decode(phrase[i..], &cp);

But we need to handle if len == 0? If invalid, break.

Return phrase[0..i].

Edge: if phrase shorter than 5 codepoints, i will be phrase.len.

